  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38137574",
      "title": "Introducing Effects",
      "lectureOrder": 698,
      "videoOrder": 643,
      "sourceHash": "1804e6e80834617cf5e52e30494e2f70a43b8d1eeab34817860942cee07fdcd9",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 4.53,
          "en": "Now with selectors out of the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.53,
          "end": 7.53,
          "en": "we now really got all these core building blocks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.53,
          "end": 11.31,
          "en": "you should know about when working with NgRx store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.31,
          "end": 14.459,
          "en": "because now you learned about Reducers and actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.459,
          "end": 17.04,
          "en": "including that alternative syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.04,
          "end": 18.66,
          "en": "which you can use for both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.66,
          "end": 20.751,
          "en": "And you learned about selectors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.751,
          "end": 24.6,
          "en": "Now I wanna really conclude this introduction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.6,
          "end": 28.74,
          "en": "by also taking a look at effects, side effects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.74,
          "end": 32.313,
          "en": "what they are and how NgRx can help you with those.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.24,
          "end": 35.97,
          "en": "So let's start with the obvious first question.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.97,
          "end": 39.75,
          "en": "What exactly is an effect or a side effect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.75,
          "end": 41.34,
          "en": "as is also called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.34,
          "end": 45.624,
          "en": "And in an Angular app in the context of using NgRx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.624,
          "end": 49.05,
          "en": "a side effect typically is anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.05,
          "end": 53.61,
          "en": "that's not directly related to an immediate UI update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.61,
          "end": 57.21,
          "en": "So for example, if you change the counter value by one end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.21,
          "end": 59.76,
          "en": "the UI therefore gets updated right away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.76,
          "end": 64.5,
          "en": "to reflect that new value, you have no side effect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.5,
          "end": 66.12,
          "en": "But you could, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.12,
          "end": 68.19,
          "en": "also be sending an HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.19,
          "end": 71.52,
          "en": "or maybe store some data in the browser or local storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.52,
          "end": 74.34,
          "en": "or maybe just log something to the console",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.34,
          "end": 78.412,
          "en": "and all these things would then be side effects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.412,
          "end": 82.67099999999999,
          "en": "Now, why is it important to be aware of such side effects?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.67099999999999,
          "end": 84.441,
          "en": "Well, because for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.441,
          "end": 88.2,
          "en": "you should avoid them in your Reducers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.2,
          "end": 92.13,
          "en": "Most importantly, your Reducer state changing functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.13,
          "end": 94.733,
          "en": "must always be synchronous.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.733,
          "end": 97.53,
          "en": "So sending an HTTP request in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.53,
          "end": 101.1,
          "en": "is absolutely not something you should do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.1,
          "end": 105.47999999999999,
          "en": "You should also not use promises or async await in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.47999999999999,
          "end": 109.11,
          "en": "Instead, these should all be pure synchronous functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.11,
          "end": 112.25999999999999,
          "en": "You should also not console log in them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.25999999999999,
          "end": 116.34,
          "en": "though of course, no horrible things will happen if you do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.34,
          "end": 120.75,
          "en": "But you should absolutely avoid sending HTTP requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.75,
          "end": 123.93,
          "en": "reaching out to local storage and things like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.93,
          "end": 128.16,
          "en": "You should keep these Reducer functions clean and simple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.16,
          "end": 130.41,
          "en": "and focused on their core job,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.41,
          "end": 134.01,
          "en": "which is to produce a new state value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.01,
          "end": 135.75,
          "en": "But of course, it is quite common",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.75,
          "end": 137.527,
          "en": "that when a certain action is dispatched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.527,
          "end": 141.111,
          "en": "you maybe also do want to log to the console",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.111,
          "end": 146.111,
          "en": "or send an HTTP request or store something in local storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.31,
          "end": 148.5,
          "en": "or get something from local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.5,
          "end": 151.86,
          "en": "All these are totally normal things to happen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.86,
          "end": 153.39,
          "en": "and that's why we'll now explore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.39,
          "end": 157.233,
          "en": "how you can handle such side effects with NgRx.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
